  {
   "url": "https://customer.aero.bombardier.com/webd/BAG/CustSite/BRAD/RACSDocument.nsf/51aae8b2b3bfdf6685256c300045ff31/ec63f8639ff3ab9d85257c1500635bd8/$FILE/ATTNBEOB.pdf/D8400-APM.pdf",
   "title": "Bombardier, Dash 8 Series 400 Airport Planning Manual (Dec 05/2014): Figure 2-2 Aircraft Dimensions, Figure 2-4 Ground Clearances, Figure 2-11 Passenger Compartment Cross Section, Figures 2-18 to 2-22 Door Clearances, Figure 2-26 Emergency Exit Locations",
   "accessed": "2026-11-16",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off Figure 2-2's side, plan and front views (tools/trace/dh8d/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The side view is drawn at the ground attitude and was turned level (1.26 degrees); the plan view is drawn turned and 0.896 times the side view's size and was rendered to its scale. The side view draws the fuselage 2.55 m tall, as the ground clearances put the crown 2.57 m over the belly (Figure 2-4) and the front view 2.59 m; the cross section prints its width (2.69 m), which the plan and front view draw. The nacelle hides 15 cabin windows in the side view: they're placed on the drawn windows' pitch. Doors' sides from each door's own clearance figure: the forward passenger (airstair) door, aft passenger door and aft baggage door on the left; the forward baggage door/Type I exit and the aft service door on the right (the service door at the passenger door's place, as its figure prints it, its opening 0.16 m shorter). Six-bladed propellers, 4.11 m across (Figure 2-26 sheet 3, Scope)."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porter_Airlines_(Dash8-400)_12.jpg",
   "title": "Porter Airlines Dash 8-400 C-GLQE, right side (Fabian Roudra Baroi, CC BY-SA 4.0)",
   "accessed": "2026-11-16",
   "note": "Checked only: the cabin window row runs unbroken behind the propeller and nacelle, at about the drawn windows' pitch (0.50 m between the forward baggage door and the aft service door), as the windows placed behind the nacelle assume. No measurement taken from it."
  }
 ],
